diff --git a/doc/performance-videotoolbox-benchmark.md b/doc/performance-videotoolbox-benchmark.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e517798
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/performance-videotoolbox-benchmark.md
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# VideoToolbox copy-versus-map experiment
+
+This is a standalone, bounded microbenchmark for an Apple Silicon Mac with
+Homebrew FFmpeg already installed. It is not part of the normal CMake build or
+test suite and does not launch Chiaki, connect to a console, change settings,
+decode video, or modify an installed application.
+
+## Status
+
+The C source compiles with C11 and `-Wall -Wextra -Werror` against FFmpeg 7.1 on
+Linux. **No Apple hardware execution or timing measurements have been obtained.**
+The attempted read-only Mac environment probe did not receive a device response.
+Consequently, this file does not claim that mapping works on the intended Mac,
+that it is faster, or that it improves Remote Play latency.
+
+## Build and run on the Mac
+
+With the standard Apple Silicon Homebrew installation:
+
+```sh
+clang -std=c11 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
+  -I/opt/homebrew/opt/ffmpeg/include scripts/benchmark-videotoolbox.c \
+  -L/opt/homebrew/opt/ffmpeg/lib -lavutil \
+  -o /tmp/chiaki-vt-benchmark
+/tmp/chiaki-vt-benchmark > /tmp/chiaki-vt-benchmark.json
+```
+
+For another Homebrew prefix, replace both include and library paths with its
+installed FFmpeg prefix. No package installation is performed by this command.
+Compile/run only this standalone program; it is not a patched app installer.
+
+## What it measures
+
+For each of NV12 and P010 at 1920×1080, the program allocates a pool of eight
+VideoToolbox frames and fills deterministic plane contents. It alternates the
+order of two operations over 50 warm-up pairs followed by 400 measured pairs:
+
+| Operation | Included work |
+| --- | --- |
+| `copy` | Allocate an AVFrame, call `av_hwframe_transfer_data`, copy frame properties |
+| `readonly_map` | Allocate an AVFrame and call `av_hwframe_map` with `AV_HWFRAME_MAP_READ` |
+
+The JSON reports p50/p95/p99/max in microseconds for preparation, and separately
+for preparation plus frame release/unmapping. Plane sampling/validation time is
+excluded. Initial device/pool allocation and filling are outside the timed loop.
+Each result is checked for format, dimensions, strides and sample pixel values.
+A separate check clones a mapped frame, releases its source-frame and original
+mapping references, then validates the retained clone before releasing it.
+
+On the success path, every output, mapping, clone and pool frame is explicitly
+freed, followed by the frames context and device references. A failure aborts
+the standalone process with an error on stderr; do not treat its possibly
+partial stdout as a completed result. Apple-specific allocation, mapping and
+unmapping behavior still requires an actual runtime test.
+
+## Limits and interpretation
+
+This uses allocated, warm VideoToolbox buffers, not buffers produced by the
+PS5 decoder under load. It excludes decoder work, GPU upload, rendering,
+presentation/compositor queues, scanout, networking and controller input. A
+smaller preparation time would be evidence for removing one CPU copy, not a
+measurement of button-to-screen improvement or complete GPU zero-copy.
+
+Before using a read-only mapping path in the app, validate NV12/P010 visual
+correctness, buffer ownership until asynchronous GPU upload finishes, buffer
+pool pressure, CoreVideo lock duration, repeated reconnect/teardown, and real
+streaming frame-time distributions on the target Mac. Keep a tested transfer
+fallback for unsupported formats or mapping failure.
